          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "For smooth autonomous $H$, let $z=(q,p)$ and let $J=\\begin{pmatrix}0&I\\\\-I&0\\end{pmatrix}$, so that $\\omega(u,v)=u^{\\mathsf T}Jv$. By step 1.1, $X_H=J\\nabla H$ and $DX_H=J K$, where $K=D^2H$ is symmetric. Hence $(DX_H)^{\\mathsf T}J+JDX_H=K^{\\mathsf T}J^{\\mathsf T}J+J^2K=K-K=0$. For a local flow map $\\phi_t$, its derivative $A(t)=D\\phi_t(z)$ exists by [F3] and satisfies $\\dot A=DX_H(\\phi_t(z))A$. Therefore $\\frac d{dt}(A^{\\mathsf T}JA)=A^{\\mathsf T}((DX_H)^{\\mathsf T}J+JDX_H)A=0$. Since $A(0)=I$, $A(t)^{\\mathsf T}JA(t)=J$, which is exactly $\\phi_t^*\\omega=\\omega$ on the actual local flow domain.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F1",
            "F3",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
