          "evidence": "Statement — Constraint consistency for a regular first-order model: Only the declared interval, open domain or parameter limit is claimed, with no extra endpoint extension. Smooth moving constraints have independent differentials on each regular slice. Fixed-endpoint chart paths on a nondegenerate compact interval and freely varied multipliers yield tangency, with autonomous constraints removing the explicit parameter derivative."
        },
