          "evidence": "Statement — Constraint consistency for a regular first-order model: No additional arbitrary selection is inferred; any inherited choice hypothesis and finite constructions retain their declared scope. Smooth moving constraints have independent differentials on each regular slice. Fixed-endpoint chart paths on a nondegenerate compact interval and freely varied multipliers yield tangency, with autonomous constraints removing the explicit parameter derivative."
        },
        {
          "case": "iff-forward",
