    "thm-rpm-h-second-class-dirac-bracket": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-countable-choice",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The **Axiom of Countable Choice**, written $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, is the following\nstatement.\n\n> For every family $(X_n)_{n \\in \\mathbb{N}}$ of nonempty sets indexed by\n> $\\mathbb{N}$ there is a function $f$ with domain $\\mathbb{N}$ such that\n> $f(n) \\in X_n$ for every $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$.\n\nEquivalently, in the vocabulary of [[def-choice-function]]: every at most\ncountable family of nonempty sets ([[def-countable]]) has a choice function.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-symplectic-form-and-symplectic-manifold",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A **symplectic form** on a smooth manifold $M$ is a smooth two-form $\\omega$\nsuch that\n\n1. $d\\omega=0$, and\n2. $(T_pM,\\omega_p)$ is a [[def-symplectic-vector-space|symplectic vector\n   space]] for every $p\\in M$.\n\nThe pair $(M,\\omega)$ is a **symplectic manifold**. Thus both closedness and\npointwise nondegeneracy are required. A zero-dimensional manifold with its\nzero two-form satisfies the definition.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "3.1",
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-smooth-functions-form-a-poisson-algebra",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "$C^\\infty(M)$, with pointwise multiplication and the symplectic Poisson\nbracket, is a real Poisson algebra.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1",
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-a-regular-level-set-is-an-embedded-submanifold",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $F:M^m\\to N^n$ be smooth, let $q\\in N$ be a regular value, and assume\n$F^{-1}(q)$ is nonempty. Then $F^{-1}(q)$ is an embedded submanifold of\ncodimension $n$. Equivalently, it has dimension $m-n$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "def-rpm-h-regular-constraint-system",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_{\\omega}$ and let $(M^{2n},\\omega)$ be a smooth symplectic manifold. A finite family of smooth functions $\\chi_1,\\ldots,\\chi_r$ defined on an open neighborhood $U\\subseteq M$ is a **regular primary constraint family** on\n\n$$C:=\\{z\\in U:\\chi_1(z)=\\cdots=\\chi_r(z)=0\\}$$\n\nwhen $d\\chi_1(z),\\ldots,d\\chi_r(z)$ are linearly independent at every $z\\in C$. The regular-level theorem [[thm-a-regular-level-set-is-an-embedded-submanifold]] then gives $C$ its embedded-submanifold structure and $T_zC=\\bigcap_a\\ker d\\chi_a(z)$. For functions $F,G$ on $U$, write $F\\approx G$ when $F|_C=G|_C$; thus $F\\approx0$ means that $F$ vanishes on $C$, without requiring it to vanish off $C$.\n\nGiven a smooth canonical Hamiltonian $H_c$ on $U$ and multiplier functions $u^a(t)$, the **total generator** is\n\n$$H_T(t,z):=H_c(t,z)+\\sum_{a=1}^r u^a(t)\\chi_a(z).$$\n\nThe functions $u^a$ are independent parameter functions; the definition does not assert that their equations determine them. If $H_c$ is an energy and $\\chi_a$ has units $[\\chi_a]$, then $u^a$ has units energy divided by $[\\chi_a]$, so every term in $H_T$ has the same units. A later constraint, if generated by consistency, is not declared primary by this definition.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "If $\\sum_a\\lambda^a d\\chi_a=0$, evaluate on each $X_{\\chi_b}$. This gives $\\sum_a\\lambda^a C_{ba}=0$ for every $b$, so invertibility implies λ=0. The differentials are independent throughout $U$; [F3] makes each nonempty joint level embedded with tangent space $TN=\\cap_a\\ker d\\chi_a$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "A1",
            "F1",
            "F3",
            "F4",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "For any $F$, set $X_F^D=X_F-X_{\\chi_a}C^{ab}\\{\\chi_b,F\\}$. Then $d\\chi_c(X_F^D)=\\{\\chi_c,F\\}-C_{ca}C^{ab}\\{\\chi_b,F\\}=0$, so it is tangent to $N$. For tangent $v$, ω$(X_F^D,v)=dF(v)$, because $d\\chi_a(v)=0$.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "A vector tangent to $N$ in the radical of $\\omega|_N$ lies in $(TN)^\\omega$, which is spanned by the independent $X_{\\chi_a}$ because the annihilator of $TN$ is spanned by independent $d\\chi_a$ and $\\omega^\\flat$ is an isomorphism. Tangency of a linear combination of these fields gives a coefficient vector annihilated by $C$, hence zero. Thus $\\omega|_N$ is nondegenerate; it is closed by pullback of $d\\omega=0$.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F1",
            "step 1.1",
            "step 2.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-4-1",
          "claim": "Contracting the tangent field $X_F^D$ with (dG) gives $X_F^D(G)=\\{G,F\\}-\\{G,\\chi_a\\}C^{ab}\\{\\chi_b,F\\}=\\{G,F\\}_D$ with the declared convention after skewness and $C^{ab}=-C^{ba}$. Since $X_F^D$ is exactly the Hamiltonian field on $N$ proved in step 2.1, the bracket is the induced symplectic Poisson bracket and obeys Jacobi by [F2] applied to the symplectic $N$. If an extension vanishes on $N$, its tangent differential vanishes, so its restricted Hamiltonian field and bracket vanish; this proves extension independence. Substitution of $F=\\chi_c$ in the formula gives zero by $CC^{-1}=I$, so constraints are Casimirs.",
          "step": "4.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "step 2.1",
            "step 3.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
