        "notes": "Invertible skew C implies independent dχ and a regular level. Projected X_F^D annihilates dχ and contracts on TN to d(F|N). Invertibility removes the radical, closure pulls back, and the induced symplectic bracket has Jacobi and extension independence. Skew inverse fixes signs; χ substitution gives Casimir zero. Empty levels are vacuous and k=0 recovers the original bracket; singular C is excluded."
