      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-25",
        "notes": "With m,c,s>0 the derivative gives p=mc V-flat/s. The Hessian kills V and is positive on its Lorentz-orthogonal complement, so rank is three. Every future shell p has inverse representative V=p-sharp; all representatives are a connected positive ray. Vertical rank three plus four base directions gives rank seven onto the embedded regular shell. Zero energy follows from degree-one homogeneity; null/zero velocities are excluded."
