      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-25",
        "notes": "Independent variations give all three shell equations; positive e and the selected nonzero future branch ensure regularity. The inverse-metric derivative and Christoffel formula yield ∇x′x′=(e′/e)x′. For m>0 auxiliary p,e have unique smooth values, and the chain rule cancels their stationary derivatives in both directions of action equivalence. dτ=em dλ gives e=1/m in proper time. For m=0 integrate dσ/dλ=e/e0>0; the transformed tangent has zero covariant acceleration, without proper time. Endpoint integration by parts is legitimate; no existence/completeness follows."
