      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Statement — Massive and null free particles in inertial time: The conclusion concerns supplied local or finite data rather than an aggregate construction over an empty index set. The flat future energy root is positive for massive states and nonzero null momenta. Constant spatial momentum gives speeds below c or equal to c in the separate branches, under the adopted actions; a zero null vector is excluded."
        },
