      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-25",
        "notes": "Direct block inversion gives g00=−N^−2, g0i=βi/N² and gij=hij−βiβj/N². Future pairing chooses the negative shell root; κ>0 for m>0 or excluded-zero null p. C_p0=κ/N>0 gives regular graph and time transversality. Coefficients are understood at (x0,q)=(ct,q). Pulling θ back gives p·qdot−H and fixed spatial endpoint variation gives Hamilton equations on the chart interval. No global gauge or endpoint continuation is claimed."
      }
