          "evidence": "Statement and step 2.2: Along a connected Hamiltonian solution interval, dH/dt=H_t. Constancy implies zero derivative; H_t vanishing along the solution implies constancy by the mean value theorem. Explicit time independence off the solution is not necessary.",
          "case_scope": {
