        "notes": "The explicit invertible linear transformation pulls the Minkowski form back to the shift-2 metric. N=1,h=δ gives temporal dx0 even though ∂0 is spacelike. p1>mc/√3 implies κ<2p1 and H<0, while p(n)=−κ and E_n>0. Since m>0, 0<p1/κ<1, so |qdot|/c=2−p1/κ>1 and observer speed is c p1/κ<c. The written extra lower bound p1/κ>1/2 is unnecessary; the preceding upper bound supplies the inequality immediately. No empirical result is asserted."
